  "stepsWireless": "1. Connect the iPhone to the Mac with a USB cable\n2. Unlock it and tap 'Trust This Computer'\n3. Press Refresh devices and check the USB badge appears",
  "stepsDeveloperMode": "1. On the iPhone: Settings → Privacy & Security → Developer Mode\n2. Turn it on and restart\n3. After the restart, tap 'Turn On' in the confirmation prompt",
  "stepsAndroidAuth": "1. Connect the phone over USB and unlock it\n2. Allow this computer in the 'Allow USB debugging' prompt\n3. If no prompt appears, enable USB debugging in Developer options",
  "stepsTeamId": "1. Find the Team ID (10 characters) at developer.apple.com/account → Membership details\n2. Enter it in Apple Team ID under Build\n3. Or tap a team of your certificates in the Signing tab",
  "stepsCertificate": "1. Xcode → Settings → Accounts: sign in with your Apple ID\n2. Manage Certificates → + → add Apple Development\n3. Press Check again",
  "stepsFlutterMissing": "1. Install the Flutter SDK from flutter.dev\n2. Add flutter/bin to PATH (~/.zshrc)\n3. Reopen the app and press Check again",
  "stepsFlutterMissingWindows": "1. Install the Flutter SDK from flutter.dev\n2. Add the flutter\\bin folder to PATH, or pick flutter.bat with \"Set tool paths…\" above\n3. Press Check again",
  "stepsXcodeMissing": "1. Install Xcode from the App Store\n2. In a terminal run sudo xcode-select -s /Applications/Xcode.app\n3. Open Xcode once and accept the license",
  "stepsAdbMissing": "1. Install the Android SDK platform-tools (Android Studio SDK Manager)\n2. Add the platform-tools folder to PATH\n3. Press Check again",
  "stepsAndroidKeystore": "1. Check the storeFile path in android/key.properties\n2. If the file is gone, recreate the keystore or fix the path\n3. For personal installs you can drop key.properties — the debug key signs the build",
  "stepsCertExpiry": "1. Xcode → Settings → Accounts → Manage Certificates: create a new Apple Development certificate\n2. Press Check again",
